This software, including its source code, templates, stylesheets, brand assets
and documentation (together, "the Software"), was written by Sandyboy Design
and Print Ltd for iPrintManage.


OWNERSHIP

The Software is owned by Sandyboy Design and Print Ltd. Nothing in this file
transfers ownership of it to anyone else.

This includes the parts that do the work of it: the page and size analysis, the
paper-size matching and bleed tolerances, the sheet, folder, tab and divider
calculations, the report, and the brand system built around them.


WHAT IPRINTMANAGE MAY DO

iPrintManage has permission to use and run the Software for its own business,
for as long as it wishes: to host it, to take client files through it, to show
it to its clients, and to have it changed on its behalf by Sandyboy Design and
Print Ltd.

This permission is given freely and is not time-limited. It is not exclusive:
Sandyboy Design and Print Ltd may continue to use, develop and license the
Software and its components elsewhere.


WHAT NEEDS PERMISSION IN WRITING

Anyone other than Sandyboy Design and Print Ltd needs its written permission
before:

  * copying, publishing or distributing the Software or any part of it,
  * selling it, licensing it, or supplying it to a third party,
  * using it as the basis of another product, whether by copying the code or by
    rewriting it from this one,
  * removing or altering the copyright notices in it.

Running the Software, and reading the source to run or maintain it, do not
need permission: they are the point of it.


NO WARRANTY

The Software is provided as it is. Sandyboy Design and Print Ltd does not
warrant that it will be free of faults or that it will be available without
interruption, and accepts no liability for loss arising from its use, so far
as the law allows. It counts pages and measures sizes to help prepare a quote;
it is not a substitute for checking a job before it goes to press.


ABOUT THIS FILE

This file records what Sandyboy Design and Print Ltd intends, and puts it
